data.content:
Three things break. Here's each one with the fix:

---

### 1. `ExecuteUpdateAsync` — no longer accepts expression trees

The setter parameter changed from `Expression<Func<…>>` to `Func<…>`. Your manual expression-tree code **won't compile**. Replace it with the much simpler non-expression lambda:

```csharp
await context.Blogs.ExecuteUpdateAsync(s =>
{
    s.SetProperty(b => b.Views, 8);
    if (nameChanged)
    {
        s.SetProperty(b => b.Name, "foo");
    }
});
```

No more `Expression.Lambda`, `Expression.Call`, etc. — conditionals go directly inside the lambda.

---

### 2. Complex type columns are now uniquified / nested paths changed

**Two related changes:**

- **Duplicate names get a numeric suffix.** `ShippingAddress.Street` and `BillingAddress.Street` previously silently shared one column; now EF appends a number (e.g. `Street` and `Street1`). This will generate a migration that renames columns and **breaks your existing schema**.

- **Nested complex types use the full path.** `Order.Payment.BillingAddress.City` previously mapped to `BillingAddress_City`; now it maps to `Payment_BillingAddress_City`.

**Fix:** Pin column names explicitly to preserve your existing schema:

```csharp
modelBuilder.Entity<Customer>(b =>
{
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.ShippingAddress, p =>
        p.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("ShippingAddress_Street"));
    b.ComplexProperty(c => c.BillingAddress, p =>
        p.Property(a => a.Street).HasColumnName("BillingAddress_Street"));
});

// For nested complex types, pin to the old (short) name:
modelBuilder.Entity<Order>()
    .ComplexProperty(o => o.Payment)
    .ComplexProperty(p => p.BillingAddress)
    .Property(a => a.City)
    .HasColumnName("BillingAddress_City");
```

---

### 3. `IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger` — new `logCommandText` parameter

Every method (`CommandReaderExecuting`, `CommandReaderExecuted`, `CommandScalarExecuting`, etc.) now requires an additional `string logCommandText` parameter. This carries the redacted SQL for logging (constants scrubbed unless `EnableSensitiveDataLogging` is on).

**Fix:** Add the parameter:

```csharp
public class MyLogger : IRelationalCommandDiagnosticsLogger
{
    public InterceptionResult<DbDataReader> CommandReaderExecuting(
        IRelationalConnection connection,
        DbCommand command,
        DbContext context,
        Guid commandId,
        Guid connectionId,
        DateTimeOffset startTime,
        string logCommandText)       // ← new parameter
    {
        // Use logCommandText for logging (redacted SQL)
        // Use command.CommandText for actual execution SQL
    }
}
```

Update **all** method overrides on the interface — they all gained this parameter.
